# ☁️ Lab 03 — Secure AWS VPC Architecture

## Public & Private Subnets with NAT Gateway and Bastion Host

This project demonstrates the design and deployment of a segmented AWS network architecture using **public and private subnets**, controlled Internet access, a **NAT Gateway**, and secure administrative access through a **Bastion Host**.

The objective was not only to deploy AWS resources, but also to understand how routing, NAT, security groups, private addressing, and SSH access work together in a cloud environment.

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of this laboratory were to:

* Design a custom Amazon VPC.
* Create public and private network segments.
* Deploy subnets across multiple Availability Zones.
* Configure Internet access for public resources.
* Provide outbound Internet connectivity to private resources.
* Prevent direct Internet exposure of private EC2 instances.
* Implement secure administrative access through a Bastion Host.
* Configure Security Group-to-Security Group access.
* Practice AWS network troubleshooting.
* Validate the architecture through real connectivity tests.

---

# 🏗️ Architecture Overview

The environment uses the following architecture:

```text
                            INTERNET
                                │
                                │
                       Internet Gateway
                                │
               ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
               │                                 │
        Public Subnet A                   Public Subnet B
         10.1.1.0/24                       10.1.2.0/24
               │
        ┌──────┴───────┐
        │              │
   Bastion Host    NAT Gateway
        │              │
        │ SSH          │ Outbound Internet
        ▼              ▲
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
               │
        Private Subnet A                 Private Subnet B
          10.1.3.0/24                      10.1.4.0/24
               │
          Private EC2
          10.1.3.217
          No Public IPv4
```

