# 🔧 Troubleshooting

Troubleshooting was an important part of this project.

## Issue 1 — Ping to Private EC2 Failed

A ping test from the Bastion Host toward the private EC2 failed.

### Cause

`ping` uses ICMP while the Private EC2 Security Group was configured to permit SSH over TCP port 22.

### Lesson

A failed ICMP test does not necessarily mean that the required application connectivity is unavailable.

Testing should focus on the protocol and port being diagnosed.

---

## Issue 2 — SSH Returned `Permission denied (publickey)`

The command:

```bash
ssh ec2-user@<PRIVATE-EC2-IP>
```

reached the private server but failed authentication.

### Analysis

This result demonstrated an important troubleshooting distinction.

```text
Connection timed out
        ↓
Possible routing / SG / NACL / connectivity issue
```

versus:

```text
Permission denied (publickey)
        ↓
Network connection successful
Authentication failed
```

The second message confirmed that TCP port 22 was reachable.

---

## Issue 3 — SSH Agent on Windows

SSH Agent Forwarding was initially considered.

However, the Windows OpenSSH Authentication Agent encountered local permission issues.

Instead of transferring the private key to the Bastion Host, SSH ProxyJump was implemented.

### Result

Successful access to the private EC2 while keeping the SSH private key on the local workstation.

